      "message": "[error] Line 145: 🔴 `send(_:)` calls `cancelReply()` before emitting `MessagePanelState.send(...)`. In PS6, `cancelReply()` now calls `discardDraftAttachments()`, which removes `.file` payloads from disk (`discardFile`) before `ConversationViewModel.send(_:)` consumes them. For reply drafts containing document/video attachments, this can dispatch paths to already-deleted files and cause send failure. Keep reply-state reset separate from attachment destruction on successful send: either (a) avoid `discardDraftAttachments()` in `cancelReply()` during send flow, or (b) emit/send first and only delete local temp files after transfer initiation succeeds.",
